{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.GeomUniversality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.GeomUniversality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomUniversality.ConditionalAudit.conditional_on_HyperbolicVolumeIndependence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomUniversality.ConditionalAudit.conditional_on_HyperbolicVolumeIndependence","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L215-L225","doc":"Witness theorem demonstrating the main proposition is conditional\non `[HyperbolicVolumeIndependence]` per CLAUDE.md §3b-cond: any two\nfunctorial evaluators are equal pointwise, recovered from the class\n(both equal the canonical volume). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomUniversality.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.volume_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomUniversality.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.volume_independent","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L210-L210","doc":"**The conjecture itself**: every functorial volume-density\nevaluator `G` that factors through the fibre functor equals the\ncanonical volume `canonicalVol` — the value is a property of the\nknot, not of the chosen evaluator.  This is the well-definedness\nbacking `m(K) = m_e · VolDensity(K, q₀)`.  `sorry` in any\nconcrete instance is understood as conjecture per §3b. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomUniversality.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.canonicalVol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomUniversality.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.canonicalVol","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L203-L203","doc":"The canonical (evaluator-independent) volume-density functional:\na function of the knot and the substrate parameter alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomUniversality.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomUniversality.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L200-L200","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomUniversality.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomUniversality.ConditionalAudit.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence","kind":"class","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L190-L213","doc":"Local stub of the conjecture's axiomatised class.  See the lake-\npackage sibling for the canonical declaration.\n\nEncodes the conjecture's content (geometric universality /\nvolume-form independence): the categorical volume-density value of\na knot is a property of the knot alone — any two functorial\nevaluators that agree pointwise yield the same volume at every\nsubstrate parameter `q`.  Stated in the shape of the claim, not as\na bare `True`.  `sorry` in any concrete instance is understood as\nconjecture per §3b. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.geom_universality_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.geom_universality_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L147-L175","doc":"**Geometric universality — conditional existence + uniqueness.**\n\nGiven a canonical `seed` that is itself functorial, the categorical\n`VolDensity` evaluator **exists** — there is some evaluator `G`\n(witnessed in the proof by `seed`) that is functorial and matches the\nseed — and is the **unique** functorial seed-matching evaluator\n(cf. `vol_density_per_knot_unique`).  Hence `m(K) = m_e · G(K, q₀)`\nis well-defined.  This is the real ∃! statement that replaces the\nearlier `True` stub; existence of the *seed itself* (Family-A linking\nweight extended to all knots) remains the open\n`prop:hoefsmit-scattering-pipeline` input.\n\nNote on the instance arguments: `[HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence]` and\n`[PLCorrectnessHypotheses]` (`conj:hyperbolic-volume-transcendence`,\n`rem:baryon-period-ratio`) are NOT used in this Lean-level\nseed-uniqueness proof — they are the named external dependencies for\nthe *geometric interpretation* of `GeomFullEval` (that the seed's\nvalues are the Thurston `Vol`/`CS` invariants), carried here so the\n§3b-cond conditional-class audit recognises the conditionality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.vol_density_subsingleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.vol_density_subsingleton","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L133-L145","doc":"**Sub-singleton companion.**  The space of VolDensity\nevaluators that match a given canonical seed and satisfy\nfunctoriality is a subsingleton.  Useful downstream as a\nSubsingleton hypothesis for `m(K)` well-definedness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.vol_density_per_knot_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.vol_density_per_knot_unique","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L111-L131","doc":"**Per-knot VolDensity uniqueness theorem (conditional).**\n\nAny two `VolDensity` evaluators that both satisfy categorical\nfunctoriality + agreement with a common canonical seed are\nequal.  Together with `HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence` +\n`PLCorrectnessHypotheses`, this gives the per-knot uniqueness\nbacking the QOU mass formula `m(K) = m_e · VolDensity(K, q₀)`.\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond: the seed-uniqueness leg is proved\nsorry-free conditional on the canonical-seed class; closing\nthe seed itself (Family-A linking-weight extension to all\nknots) is the open `prop:hoefsmit-scattering-pipeline` work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullCanonicalSeed.matches_seed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullCanonicalSeed.matches_seed","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L109-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullCanonicalSeed.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullCanonicalSeed.mk","kind":"ctor","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L107-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullCanonicalSeed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullCanonicalSeed","kind":"class","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L100-L109","doc":"**Canonical normalisation seed.**  The VolDensity evaluator\nagrees pointwise with a fixed reference evaluator `seed` on\nevery knot.  In production this seed is the Family-A\nlinking-weight evaluation at the Borromean 𝓑₃ (the framework's\ncanonical reference) extended functorially to all knots; the\nclass is parametrised by `seed` to keep the substrate model\nabstract. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullFunctorial.factors_per_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullFunctorial.factors_per_block","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L97-L97","doc":"Stage-4 functorial factorisation: the evaluator is the geometric\nprojection times the per-block sum (the paper's forced form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullFunctorial.perBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullFunctorial.perBlock","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L94-L94","doc":"The knot's own per-block Markov-trace sum\n`Σ_λ w_λ χ_λ(β_K)/dim λ`, over the partitions of the knot's OWN\nHecke level (H₃ for the 3-strand Borromean baryons). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullFunctorial.geomLeading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullFunctorial.geomLeading","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L90-L90","doc":"The geometric-projection factor (Vol(K)/ℏ_q² for hyperbolic K). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullFunctorial.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullFunctorial.mk","kind":"ctor","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullFunctorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullFunctorial","kind":"class","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L62-L98","doc":"**Categorical functoriality (axiomatised).**  The VolDensity\nevaluator factors through the fibre functor of the QOU\nsubstrate's monoidal category — equivalently, it respects\nHecke-algebra morphisms.  Concretely (`prop:hoefsmit-scattering-\npipeline` Stage 3–4), this functoriality means the evaluator\nfactors as the geometric projection `geomLeading` (= Vol(K)/ℏ_q²\nfor hyperbolic K) times the knot's OWN per-block Markov-trace sum\n`perBlock K q = Σ_λ w_λ χ_λ(β_K)/dim λ`:\n\n    G K q = geomLeading K q · perBlock K q.\n\n**Replaces the previous trivial `functorial : True` stub\n(2026-06-01).**  The class now carries the real Stage-4 per-block\nfactorisation as its content.  This is the structural statement\nthat production's `vol_density_borromean` VIOLATES — it drops the\nper-block factor `perBlock` and substitutes a global H₄ scalar\n(the discrepancy is quantified, raw, in\n`vol-density-per-block-wiring.witness.json`: the H₃ per-block trace\n`tr_M(proton) ≈ 1.065` differs from the global scalar `≈ 2.53` by\n`≈ 2.38×`).\n\n**Open math.**  The conjectural join is the Yekutieli non-abelian\nStokes identification `perBlock = boundary-holonomy of the\ncategorical connection` (`conj:geom-yekutieli-alignment`); that\njoin is the §3b-cond axiom carried by the class instance, not a\nLean-proved fact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullEval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomFullEval","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L56-L60","doc":"A per-knot VolDensity evaluator: takes a knot/link\nrepresentative `K` (abstracted as a generic type to avoid\ncommitting to a specific knot encoding here) and the\nsubstrate parameter `q`, returns the categorical volume in ℝ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PLCorrectnessHypotheses.pl_decomposition_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PLCorrectnessHypotheses.pl_decomposition_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PLCorrectnessHypotheses.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PLCorrectnessHypotheses.mk","kind":"ctor","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L21-L21","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PLCorrectnessHypotheses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PLCorrectnessHypotheses","kind":"class","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L20-L23","doc":"**§3b-cond hypothesis class** for `conj:baryon-period-ratio`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.pairing_unitary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.pairing_unitary","kind":"theorem","line":15,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L15-L15","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":14,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L14-L14","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence","kind":"class","line":13,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/geom-universality.lean#L13-L18","doc":"**§3b-cond hypothesis class** for `conj:hyperbolic-volume-transcendence`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}